== Operations

The Operations phase covers the security responsibilities that continue after a product or service is released. Its controls apply throughout both the active development period and the support period.

.*What this phase covers*
[%collapsible]
====
[mermaid]
----
flowchart LR
    T[Third-party watch] --> U[Updates applied and distributed]
    E[Environment protection]
----

* *Third-party watch* — continuously identify and assess vulnerabilities in third-party components, and track the security updates that suppliers publish for them.
* *Updates applied and distributed* — ensure that the relevant updates are actually applied to your own systems and delivered onward to product users.
* *Environment protection* — keep development, test, staging and production environments separated, hardened, access-controlled and monitored, and handle production data safely.

The controls listed below are the authoritative scope of this phase. Installed extension modules may add further controls here.
====

=== Why it matters

Security does not end at release. New vulnerabilities in third-party components emerge continuously, and unpatched environments become easy targets. These controls ensure that your team stays on top of emerging threats and keeps infrastructure protected for as long as the product is in use.

